  "title": "The creation map splits by atom",
  "subject": "How native creation in a space with several handles depends on its atoms",
  "conclusion": "In a space made of plane glue and atoms at 3-edge cuts, whether a removal creates at a gluing line depends only on the atoms holding the two lines, since every other atom acts as the vertex it replaced (proved for atoms attached at a point, checked exactly for atoms attached at a line on 13 designs). So each removal's halo is its own atom's, and atoms attached at a line have no halo on plane glue.",
